    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171-a4">

                <pb facs="0422" n="338" xml:id="pg338"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in Mr. Phelan’s No.
                    82.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Scott to Mr.
                            Phelan.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canadian Government S. S. Lansdowne</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Digby, Nova Scotia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1886-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi>
                            11, 1886</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your letter of this
                    day’s date, requiring to know why I have detained the American fishing schooner
                    D. J. Adams, and in reply would beg of you to apply to the deputy minister of
                    fisheries in Ottawa for an answer, as I am acting under instruction.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. A. SCOTT,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Commanding the
                            Marine Police.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Hon. M. H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phelan</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General for the United States.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
